Falsifies `program_argument_contract::verification::finish_zeros_every_byte_past_the_last_record`.

The defect: `finish` writes the header and leaves the bytes past the last record as they were, so
a page reused for a shorter line still holds the longer line's bytes after its records.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(page[at], 0)`, on the stale `0xa5` bytes past the
one record.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -210,8 +210,6 @@
         // `used` never passes `MAXIMUM_RECORDS_BYTES`, which the assertion above keeps inside a `u32`.
         #[allow(clippy::cast_possible_truncation)]
         let total = self.used as u32;
-        // Past the records, the page holds zeros and nothing of an earlier line.
-        self.page[HEADER_BYTES + self.used..].fill(0);
         self.page[8..12].copy_from_slice(&self.count.to_le_bytes());
         self.page[12..16].copy_from_slice(&total.to_le_bytes());
         self.page[..8].copy_from_slice(&MAGIC);
